== attempt_87 finished: exit 2, outcome fail, 138 s
== reset agent gave up: reset.py can't reset the drawer as it sits now: it is in the slot the right way round but pushed about 2.0–2.2 cm past flush, and this gripper can't grip its pull tab there. A person needs to pull the drawer out to about flush. From there the existing reset works: the tab pinch and pull (attempt 17), the extraction (attempts 18 and 28), and the placement with the pull facing the robot (attempts 74 and 77).

**What I tried on the robot (attempts 84–87, all failed):**
- **Attempt 84:** ran before your 16:50 change. With the old 3 cm slot allowance the model check refused every pinch position, and the run stopped cleanly without touching anything.
- **Attempts 85–87:** with the 5 cm allowance, I tried 12 pinch positions with level fingers, under three geometries. Every one passed the model check and every one closed on nothing (gripper reading 90). The approaches pressed on something at 21–42 N.
- **What the wrist images show:** with the fingertips 7 mm higher, the pads landed on the label plate. With other settings the fingers' forward edge pressed the drawer face; the real face is about 3.1 cm deep (2.0–2.2 cm from the side camera plus the 1.1 cm side-to-wrist offset measured at flush).

**Why it doesn't fit:**
- The tab hangs about 7 mm above the slot floor (floor of the opening at 1.5 cm, tab bottom at about 2.25 cm).
- The label plate sits right above the tab, and the drawer face is right behind it.
- The tilted finger pad is about 17 mm tall, so it would have to fit between floor and plate with almost no margin. The camera estimates are only good to a few millimetres.
- At this depth the wrist camera can't tell whether the tab is between the pads or beyond the fingertips. At flush it worked only after diagnosing exactly that from wrist images.

**What the program does now (commit 8f6fe43):**
- **Recognises the recessed state:** it measures the median depth of the drawer face in the slot opening. An empty slot reads much deeper.
- **Recess up to 1.2 cm:** it pinches the tab shifted deeper by the recess and pulls it out. This passed the model check offline and in a dry run, but has never been tried on the robot.
- **Deeper recess:** the run stops at once, before any motion, with "drawer pushed X m past flush … pull it out to about flush by hand".
- **Also in this commit:** the release after a pull is 0.65, and a missed deep pinch now lifts straight up.

**Not tried:** pressing on the tab with a fingertip and dragging the drawer out by friction. Its success rate is unpredictable and it would push hard near the cabinet.

The RL policy pushes up to 2 cm past the plane, so this state will come back. Options:
- have the RL episode stop pushing at flush;
- add a stop inside the slot;
- or use a different tool for the pull.

Notes are in `notes/notes.md`.
