== reset agent gave up: reset.py can't fix the current scene. The drawer is in the slot pushed about 2.1 cm past flush (median 21.4 mm from side depth) — attempt 89, the reset at 21:17. A person needs to pull it out to about flush, then resets can continue.

**What the program did (attempt 89):** it recognised the recessed drawer, moved only to the ready pose and home, and stopped with "drawer pushed 0.021 m past flush … a person must pull it out to about flush". That's the intended behaviour, not a bug. Repeating the run would only repeat the stop.

**Why it can't pull at 2 cm:** attempts 85–87 tried 12 pinch positions at 2.0–2.2 cm recess, even with a 5 cm allowance. Every one closed on nothing, and the fingers pressed on the label plate, the drawer face or the slot floor at 21–42 N. The tab hangs about 7 mm above the slot floor, with the plate right above it and the face right behind it. With the allowance now 2 cm, the plate window for your hook idea sits about 3.5 cm deep, so the model check refuses it before any motion.

**After the drawer is pulled to about flush:** the reset goes through the tab pinch and pull, extraction, and placement with the pull facing the robot. Each of these steps has worked on the robot.

**This state is recurring:** your 2 cm keep-out was meant to stop the RL push from recessing the drawer more than about 1 cm, but here it read 2.1 cm after an episode. Something on the RL side (the push depth or the drawer's travel) still lets it go deeper. The reset can only handle recesses up to 1.5 cm: up to 1.2 cm it checks out in offline model checks and an earlier dry run, from 1.2 to 1.5 cm offline only, and none of it has been run on the robot.

**Change in this commit:** only the stop message, which now names the 2 cm allowance (latest commit d2bf659). Notes are in `notes/notes.md`.
