== attempt_99 finished: exit 0, outcome success, 183 s
== reset agent done: Attempt 99 (commit ecd7fd7) worked on the robot. The drawer was placed 2.7 cm from the target (tolerance 5 cm). The vision judge confirmed the pull wall faces the robot (confidence 0.85), and the orchestrator's layout check passed.

What went wrong in attempt 98: the drawer was not in the slot at all. It was standing on the table, pressed against the cabinet front. Table detection lumped it in with the cabinet, so the program thought it was a drawer sticking out of the slot and clamped the wall edge, which pulled nothing.

The fix: points 4-12 mm above the table in front of the cabinet now count as a drawer on the table, because a drawer in the slot hangs at least 1.5 cm up. The program outlines it from its wall tops and picks it up from the table as usual. Each run now also saves the side-camera point clouds (cloud_<tag>.npy) so failures can be replayed offline.

Not yet tested on the robot: the new handling for a drawer about 1 cm out (tab pinch, or edge clamp at 2-4 cm), because the drawer was never in that state in these runs.
